{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"f109e3f3bb10220d","name":"card_unit_m20_scout_car","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/CovertOp/units/card_unit_m20_scout_car","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"M20 SCOUT CAR","text":"Deployment: Target a unit. \r\nDestruction: It gets +1+1.","flavorText":"The M20 Armored Utility Car, also known as the M20 Scout Car, was a variant of the Greyhound armored vehicle. The M20 had the turret replaced by a low-profile armored open-top structure and an anti-aircraft ring mounting a .50 cal M2 heavy machine gun. To address its lack of anti-tank weaponry, the crew was equipped with a bazooka. The M20 was primarily used for command purposes and reconnaissance, but it also functioned as an armored personnel carrier and cargo transporter. The vehicle was known for its speed and maneuverability, and on top of that it offered some protection against small arms fire and shrapnel. When used in command roles it had additional radio equipment installed. Originally it was named the M10 Armored Utility Car, but it was later re-designated as the M20 to prevent confusion with the 3-inch Gun Motor Carriage M10. Ford produced a total of 3,680 M20’s during its two-year production period from 1943 to 1944.","faction":"USA","type":"tank","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":1,"operationCost":1,"attack":1,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_m20_scout_car","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_m20_scout_car_title","SourceString":"M20 SCOUT CAR","LocalizedString":"M20 SCOUT CAR"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::tank","attack":1,"defense":3,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_m20_scout_car_text","SourceString":"Deployment: Target a unit. \r\nDestruction: It gets +1+1.","LocalizedString":"Deployment: Target a unit. \r\nDestruction: It gets +1+1."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_m20_scout_car_history","SourceString":"The M20 Armored Utility Car, also known as the M20 Scout Car, was a variant of the Greyhound armored vehicle. The M20 had the turret replaced by a low-profile armored open-top structure and an anti-aircraft ring mounting a .50 cal M2 heavy machine gun. To address its lack of anti-tank weaponry, the crew was equipped with a bazooka. The M20 was primarily used for command purposes and reconnaissance, but it also functioned as an armored personnel carrier and cargo transporter. The vehicle was known for its speed and maneuverability, and on top of that it offered some protection against small arms fire and shrapnel. When used in command roles it had additional radio equipment installed. Originally it was named the M10 Armored Utility Car, but it was later re-designated as the M20 to prevent confusion with the 3-inch Gun Motor Carriage M10. Ford produced a total of 3,680 M20’s during its two-year production period from 1943 to 1944.","LocalizedString":"The M20 Armored Utility Car, also known as the M20 Scout Car, was a variant of the Greyhound armored vehicle. The M20 had the turret replaced by a low-profile armored open-top structure and an anti-aircraft ring mounting a .50 cal M2 heavy machine gun. To address its lack of anti-tank weaponry, the crew was equipped with a bazooka. The M20 was primarily used for command purposes and reconnaissance, but it also functioned as an armored personnel carrier and cargo transporter. The vehicle was known for its speed and maneuverability, and on top of that it offered some protection against small arms fire and shrapnel. When used in command roles it had additional radio equipment installed. Originally it was named the M10 Armored Utility Car, but it was later re-designated as the M20 to prevent confusion with the 3-inch Gun Motor Carriage M10. Ford produced a total of 3,680 M20’s during its two-year production period from 1943 to 1944."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetE